---
import { COMMIT_SHA } from 'astro:env/server';
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

const repo = 'https://github.com/ayagmar/ayagmar.dev';
const isCommit = /^[0-9a-f]{40}$/.test(COMMIT_SHA);
---

<Base
  title="Colophon"
  description="How min7 is built and served: Astro, Svelte, Cloudflare Workers and Pagefind, and the commit this build came from."
>
  <div class="paper column t-colophon">
    <h1>Colophon</h1>
    <p>
      Built with Astro and Svelte, served by Cloudflare Workers. Search by Pagefind. No tracking, no
      cookies, no third-party scripts.
    </p>
    <p>
      Comments under posts and notes are GitHub Discussions, shown by{' '}
      <a href="https://giscus.app/">giscus</a>. They load from giscus.app only when you press "Show
      comments".
    </p>
    <p>
      This build:
      {isCommit ? (
        <a href={`${repo}/commit/${COMMIT_SHA}`}>
          <code>{COMMIT_SHA.slice(0, 12)}</code>
        </a>
      ) : (
        <code>{COMMIT_SHA}</code>
      )}
    </p>
    <p>
      Set in Source Serif 4, with JetBrains Mono for dates, numbers and code, both self-hosted. The
      room on the home page is drawn by a script, pixel by pixel; no photos. It is the only picture
      on the site; the rest is type and hairlines.
    </p>
    <p><a href={repo}>Source</a> (code MIT, writing all rights reserved).</p>
    <p>
      Weather data by <a href="https://open-meteo.com/">Open-Meteo</a>{' '}
      (<a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/">CC BY 4.0</a>); simplified
      visualization. It is Rabat's weather, shown in the room's window on the home page.
    </p>
  </div>
</Base>
